351
00:20:47,050 --> 00:20:48,339
A11Y-001 · 4.

352
00:20:48,339 --> 00:20:51,779
Releasing it without breaking hundreds of call sites

353
00:20:52,904 --> 00:20:57,874
The other changes (native button, aria-hidden icon, aria-disabled) fix behaviour without changing the

354
00:20:57,874 --> 00:21:02,462
API, so they can ship immediately in a minor or patch release.

355
00:21:02,462 --> 00:21:07,815
Mention them in the changelog: teams with styles targeting the internal div will notice.

356
00:21:09,190 --> 00:21:11,293
A11Y-001 · Follow-up 1

357
00:21:12,417 --> 00:21:15,697
A team wants a tooltip on every icon button.

358
00:21:15,697 --> 00:21:18,977
How does a tooltip relate to the accessible name,

359
00:21:18,977 --> 00:21:21,893
and how should it behave for keyboard users?

360
00:21:27,050 --> 00:21:29,853
A tooltip supplies supplemental explanation; the icon button

361
00:21:29,853 --> 00:21:32,306
still needs a name before it appears.

362
00:21:32,306 --> 00:21:35,810
Show it on keyboard focus as well as pointer hover,

363
00:21:35,810 --> 00:21:40,015
allow Escape to dismiss it, and avoid moving focus into a noninteractive

364
00:21:40,015 --> 00:21:40,366
tooltip.

365
00:21:40,366 --> 00:21:43,870
Associate useful descriptive content without making the name unexpectedly verbose.

366
00:21:43,870 --> 00:21:47,725
Ensure hoverable, dismissible, and persistent behavior where the content criterion applies.

367
00:21:47,725 --> 00:21:51,229
If the popup contains interactive controls, it is a different

368
00:21:51,229 --> 00:21:54,733
pattern and should not be presented as a simple tooltip.

369
00:21:56,109 --> 00:21:58,343
A11Y-001 · Follow-up 2

370
00:21:59,469 --> 00:22:02,958
When is aria-labelledby better than aria-label here?

371
00:22:08,339 --> 00:22:13,181
Use labelledby when visible text already provides the intended label or when combining

372
00:22:13,181 --> 00:22:17,651
a visible action with contextual text is clearer than duplicating a string.

373
00:22:17,651 --> 00:22:22,867
It keeps spoken wording aligned with the visible interface and can improve localization maintenance.

374
00:22:22,867 --> 00:22:25,474
The referenced elements need stable unique identifiers.

375
00:22:25,474 --> 00:22:30,689
Use aria-label for an otherwise unnamed icon control when no suitable visible text exists.

376
00:22:30,689 --> 00:22:33,669
Do not add both casually and assume both

377
00:22:33,669 --> 00:22:36,649
will be spoken; naming precedence determines the result.

378
00:22:38,025 --> 00:22:40,173
A11Y-001 · Follow-up 3

379
00:22:41,298 --> 00:22:44,236
How would you test, automatically, that every icon

380
00:22:44,236 --> 00:22:46,808
button in a product has a name?

381
00:22:52,194 --> 00:22:55,773
Run an accessibility scanner in the rendered product and add

382
00:22:55,773 --> 00:22:59,353
a browser test that queries buttons by their accessible name.

383
00:22:59,353 --> 00:23:03,290
Cover states where icons or labels change and multiple component instances.

384
00:23:03,290 --> 00:23:05,796
Required input typing can help library consumers,

385
00:23:05,796 --> 00:23:09,018
but an empty string can still pass a string

386
00:23:09,018 --> 00:23:09,376
type.

387
00:23:09,376 --> 00:23:13,313
Add runtime development diagnostics or tests for empty labels where useful.

388
00:23:13,313 --> 00:23:15,819
Automated checks establish that a name exists,

389
00:23:15,819 --> 00:23:19,399
not that every name is meaningful, so review representative wording

390
00:23:19,399 --> 00:23:20,114
as well.

