00:24:31,369 --> 00:24:33,133
A11Y-002 · Interview question

412
00:24:34,259 --> 00:24:37,513
What does a modal dialog have to do for keyboard and

413
00:24:37,513 --> 00:24:40,471
screen-reader users, and which of those does this one do?

414
00:24:40,471 --> 00:24:42,838
Fix it, and explain the second team's bug.

415
00:24:49,488 --> 00:24:51,155
A11Y-002 · Answer

416
00:24:52,280 --> 00:24:55,893
A modal dialog must: move focus into itself when it opens,

417
00:24:55,893 --> 00:24:59,506
keep keyboard focus and screen-reader browsing inside, have an accessible name,

418
00:24:59,506 --> 00:25:03,448
close on Escape, and return focus to where the user was when

419
00:25:03,448 --> 00:25:04,105
it closes.

420
00:25:04,105 --> 00:25:06,076
This one does none of them.

421
00:25:07,452 --> 00:25:08,724
A11Y-002 · 1.

422
00:25:08,724 --> 00:25:09,995
Focus stays behind

423
00:25:11,121 --> 00:25:13,028
Opening it does not move focus.

424
00:25:13,028 --> 00:25:15,890
A keyboard user's next Tab goes to whatever followed

425
00:25:15,890 --> 00:25:18,433
the trigger, and a screen-reader user hears nothing.

426
00:25:18,433 --> 00:25:20,977
The user may not know a dialog opened.

427
00:25:22,352 --> 00:25:23,600
A11Y-002 · 2.

428
00:25:23,600 --> 00:25:26,930
The rest of the page is still reachable

429
00:25:28,055 --> 00:25:32,456
Nothing stops Tab from leaving the dialog, and nothing hides the page

430
00:25:32,456 --> 00:25:36,857
behind it from assistive technology. role="dialog" alone does not make anything modal.

431
00:25:38,232 --> 00:25:39,691
A11Y-002 · 3.

432
00:25:39,691 --> 00:25:41,150
No accessible name

433
00:25:42,275 --> 00:25:46,809
role="dialog" with no aria-labelledby or aria-label is announced as just "dialog".

434
00:25:46,809 --> 00:25:51,757
The heading is right there; it needs an id and a reference.

435
00:25:53,132 --> 00:25:54,217
A11Y-002 · 4.

436
00:25:54,217 --> 00:25:58,196
No keyboard way to close, and focus is lost on close

437
00:25:59,321 --> 00:26:03,993
There is no Escape handling, and the close control is a <span>: not focusable,

438
00:26:03,993 --> 00:26:08,665
not a button, and its only text, ×, is announced as "times" or "multiplication".

439
00:26:08,665 --> 00:26:12,670
When the dialog closes, its content is destroyed while it contains focus,

440
00:26:12,670 --> 00:26:17,343
so focus falls back to <body> and the user has to find their place

441
00:26:17,343 --> 00:26:17,676
again.

442
00:26:19,052 --> 00:26:22,660
A11Y-002 · Fix: use the native <dialog> element

443
00:26:23,786 --> 00:26:28,378
showModal() gives most of this for free: the dialog renders in the top layer,

444
00:26:28,378 --> 00:26:32,971
the rest of the document becomes inert (unreachable by Tab and hidden from assistive

445
00:26:32,971 --> 00:26:36,908
technology), focus moves into the dialog, and Escape fires a cancel event.

446
00:26:36,908 --> 00:26:39,532
The component then only needs to name it,

447
00:26:39,532 --> 00:26:42,157
provide a real close button, and restore focus.

