493
00:29:29,401 --> 00:29:33,814
and runs its lifecycle hooks, whether or not the dialog ever shows it.

494
00:29:33,814 --> 00:29:37,888
That is why the hidden form makes HTTP requests on page load.

495
00:29:37,888 --> 00:29:41,622
The fixed version renders the content all the time inside a

496
00:29:41,622 --> 00:29:45,356
closed <dialog> (which is hidden), so the cost is the same.

497
00:29:46,732 --> 00:29:48,098
A11Y-002 · 5.

498
00:29:48,098 --> 00:29:52,198
The second team's bug: projected content is always created

499
00:29:53,323 --> 00:29:57,617
For heavy or lazy content, the library should offer one of:

500
00:29:58,992 --> 00:30:00,194
A11Y-002 · 5.

501
00:30:00,194 --> 00:30:03,801
The second team's bug: projected content is always created

502
00:30:04,926 --> 00:30:07,918
A template slot: the consumer passes an <ng-template>,

503
00:30:07,918 --> 00:30:11,284
and the dialog renders it with ngTemplateOutlet only while

504
00:30:11,284 --> 00:30:11,658
open.

505
00:30:11,658 --> 00:30:14,650
A dialog service that creates the content component

506
00:30:14,650 --> 00:30:17,268
on demand (the CDK Dialog does this).

507
00:30:17,268 --> 00:30:21,757
Consumers can also wrap their content in @defer or their own @if.

508
00:30:23,132 --> 00:30:25,234
A11Y-002 · Follow-up 1

509
00:30:26,359 --> 00:30:30,414
A team wants clicking the backdrop to close the dialog.

510
00:30:30,414 --> 00:30:35,686
How would you implement it with <dialog>, and should it be the default?

511
00:30:40,637 --> 00:30:43,789
Detect a pointer interaction outside the dialog's content rectangle

512
00:30:43,789 --> 00:30:46,941
and route it through the component's normal close request.

513
00:30:46,941 --> 00:30:50,444
A dialog-target click alone can also occur in content padding,

514
00:30:50,444 --> 00:30:54,647
so account for geometry and pointer down/up behavior to avoid accidental closure

515
00:30:54,647 --> 00:30:55,347
after dragging.

516
00:30:55,347 --> 00:30:59,200
Make backdrop dismissal an explicit policy rather than a universal default.

517
00:30:59,200 --> 00:31:02,703
A destructive confirmation or unsaved form may require deliberate cancellation.

518
00:31:02,703 --> 00:31:05,505
Keep Escape and a visible close or cancel

519
00:31:05,505 --> 00:31:07,956
control available according to the product's requirements.

520
00:31:09,332 --> 00:31:11,415
A11Y-002 · Follow-up 2

521
00:31:12,540 --> 00:31:16,359
Which element should receive focus first in a destructive confirmation dialog?

522
00:31:16,359 --> 00:31:16,707
Why?

523
00:31:21,990 --> 00:31:24,859
Usually focus the least destructive action so an

524
00:31:24,859 --> 00:31:27,728
accidental Enter does not commit the destructive operation.

525
00:31:27,728 --> 00:31:30,598
If the dialog begins with important structured information,

526
00:31:30,598 --> 00:31:35,261
focus a static heading or paragraph with tabindex minus one so the content

527
00:31:35,261 --> 00:31:36,695
can be read first.

528
00:31:36,695 --> 00:31:39,565
Choose according to the task rather than always

529
00:31:39,565 --> 00:31:42,076
focusing the first element in DOM order.

530
00:31:42,076 --> 00:31:46,739
Give the dialog a meaningful name and ensure the destructive action is clear.

531
00:31:46,739 --> 00:31:51,401
Confirm focus restoration and a sensible fallback if the invoking item is deleted.

532
00:31:52,777 --> 00:31:54,968
A11Y-002 · Follow-up 3

533
00:31:56,093 --> 00:32:00,931
How would you test focus return and background inertness in an automated test?

534
00:32:06,360 --> 00:32:10,486
In a real browser, focus the invoking button, open the modal,

535
00:32:10,486 --> 00:32:15,362
verify focus enters, and press Tab and Shift Tab to ensure background controls

536
00:32:15,362 --> 00:32:16,112
are unreachable.

537
00:32:16,112 --> 00:32:19,863
Press Escape and verify the model closes and focus returns.

538
00:32:19,863 --> 00:32:22,864
Try programmatically focusing a background control while the

539
00:32:22,864 --> 00:32:25,490
modal is open to check native inertness.

540
00:32:25,490 --> 00:32:27,741
Cover close-button and form-dialog paths too.

541
00:32:27,741 --> 00:32:31,117
DOM attributes alone do not prove native modality; showModal

542
00:32:31,117 --> 00:32:34,117
and actual interaction are the behavior under test.

