00:34:19,373 --> 00:34:21,313
A11Y-003 · Interview question

571
00:34:22,438 --> 00:34:25,363
Describe how tabs should behave for keyboard and screen-reader

572
00:34:25,363 --> 00:34:28,289
users, list what is missing, and fix the component.

573
00:34:28,289 --> 00:34:30,890
Point out any bug that only appears because

574
00:34:30,890 --> 00:34:33,491
there are two tab groups on the page.

575
00:34:40,141 --> 00:34:41,844
A11Y-003 · Answer

576
00:34:42,969 --> 00:34:47,332
The WAI-ARIA tabs pattern: a tablist contains tab elements, each controlling a tabpanel.

577
00:34:47,332 --> 00:34:52,032
Only the selected tab is in the Tab order (a roving tabindex); arrow keys

578
00:34:52,032 --> 00:34:56,395
move between tabs, and Home and End jump to the first and last.

579
00:34:56,395 --> 00:34:58,745
Each tab says whether it is selected,

580
00:34:58,745 --> 00:35:01,431
and each panel is labelled by its tab.

581
00:35:02,806 --> 00:35:04,400
A11Y-003 · 1.

582
00:35:04,400 --> 00:35:06,526
No roles or states

583
00:35:07,651 --> 00:35:10,581
Divs with click handlers expose nothing.

584
00:35:10,581 --> 00:35:16,932
A screen reader announces plain text, not "Security, tab, 2 of 2, selected".

585
00:35:16,932 --> 00:35:23,771
Needed: role="tablist" (with a label), role="tab" with aria-selected and aria-controls, and role="tabpanel" with aria-labelledby.

586
00:35:25,146 --> 00:35:26,474
A11Y-003 · 2.

587
00:35:26,474 --> 00:35:27,802
Not keyboard operable

588
00:35:28,927 --> 00:35:31,401
The tabs are not focusable at all.

589
00:35:31,401 --> 00:35:35,291
Making each one a plain <button> would fix reachability but produce

590
00:35:35,291 --> 00:35:39,180
the wrong pattern: five Tab presses to get past five tabs.

591
00:35:39,180 --> 00:35:42,362
Only the selected tab should have tabindex="0"; the rest

592
00:35:42,362 --> 00:35:45,191
get -1, and arrow keys move between them.

593
00:35:46,565 --> 00:35:48,056
A11Y-003 · 3.

594
00:35:48,056 --> 00:35:50,044
Duplicate ids across instances

595
00:35:51,170 --> 00:35:53,708
Both groups render id="tab-0" and id="tab-1".

596
00:35:53,708 --> 00:35:58,361
Duplicate ids are invalid, and any aria-labelledby or aria-controls reference resolves

597
00:35:58,361 --> 00:36:01,322
to the first match in the document,

598
00:36:01,322 --> 00:36:05,976
so the second group's panels would be labelled by the first

599
00:36:05,976 --> 00:36:06,822
group's tabs.

600
00:36:06,822 --> 00:36:10,206
Ids must be unique per instance: generate them

601
00:36:10,206 --> 00:36:13,591
from a counter, never from the position alone.

602
00:36:14,966 --> 00:36:16,252
A11Y-003 · 4.

603
00:36:16,252 --> 00:36:17,966
Nothing is selected initially

604
00:36:19,092 --> 00:36:23,094
No tab starts active, so every panel is hidden until a click.

605
00:36:23,094 --> 00:36:26,429
With a roving tabindex, no tab would be focusable either,

606
00:36:26,429 --> 00:36:29,431
and the whole component would be unreachable by keyboard.

607
00:36:30,806 --> 00:36:32,116
A11Y-003 · 5.

608
00:36:32,116 --> 00:36:34,737
State is pushed into children imperatively

609
00:36:35,862 --> 00:36:38,139
select writes into each child's signal.

610
00:36:38,139 --> 00:36:43,455
If tabs are added or removed (@if around a <ui-tab>), nothing updates their state.

611
00:36:43,455 --> 00:36:48,011
Deriving "am I selected?" from one source in the parent avoids that.

