00:39:52,966 --> 00:39:55,290
A11Y-003 · Fixed version

661
00:39:56,415 --> 00:40:01,451
This uses automatic activation: moving with the arrow keys also selects the tab.

662
00:40:01,451 --> 00:40:03,775
That suits panels that render instantly.

663
00:40:03,775 --> 00:40:07,262
If showing a panel is slow (it fetches data),

664
00:40:07,262 --> 00:40:09,974
use manual activation instead: arrows move focus,

665
00:40:09,974 --> 00:40:11,911
and Enter or Space selects.

666
00:40:13,286 --> 00:40:15,432
A11Y-003 · Fixed version

667
00:40:16,556 --> 00:40:19,518
The panel has tabindex="0" so keyboard users can

668
00:40:19,518 --> 00:40:22,479
reach a panel that has no focusable content.

669
00:40:22,479 --> 00:40:27,290
If every panel always starts with a focusable element, that can be dropped.

670
00:40:28,666 --> 00:40:31,994
A11Y-003 · What a strong candidate also mentions

671
00:40:33,119 --> 00:40:37,341
Right-to-left layouts reverse the meaning of the left and right arrow keys.

672
00:40:37,341 --> 00:40:41,212
Read the direction (for example with the CDK Directionality) instead of

673
00:40:41,212 --> 00:40:45,083
hard-coding it. - selectedIndex as a model() lets consumers control the

674
00:40:45,083 --> 00:40:48,601
selected tab, for example to sync it with the URL.

675
00:40:48,601 --> 00:40:52,472
The label input is required, so a tablist is never nameless.

676
00:40:52,472 --> 00:40:55,287
Adding it to an existing component is breaking,

677
00:40:55,287 --> 00:40:57,751
so it would be staged (see A11Y-001).

678
00:40:59,126 --> 00:41:01,430
A11Y-003 · Follow-up 1

679
00:41:02,555 --> 00:41:06,011
When would you choose manual activation over automatic activation?

680
00:41:11,400 --> 00:41:15,259
Use manual activation when showing a panel is slow or

681
00:41:15,259 --> 00:41:18,733
costly, such as a network request or heavy render.

682
00:41:18,733 --> 00:41:22,206
Arrows move focus, while Enter or Space commits selection.

683
00:41:22,206 --> 00:41:25,294
Automatic activation is appropriate when panel changes are

684
00:41:25,294 --> 00:41:27,996
immediate and moving through tabs remains responsive.

685
00:41:27,996 --> 00:41:33,399
Keep focused and selected indices separate for manual activation and document the keyboard model.

686
00:41:33,399 --> 00:41:38,031
Do not change between models unpredictably based on a transient request duration.

687
00:41:39,406 --> 00:41:41,671
A11Y-003 · Follow-up 2

688
00:41:42,796 --> 00:41:45,099
The tabs overflow on a phone.

689
00:41:45,099 --> 00:41:49,705
What happens to keyboard and screen-reader behaviour if you add scroll buttons?

690
00:41:55,112 --> 00:41:59,263
Keep tab roles, selection, panel relationships, and the one-tab-stop strategy intact.

691
00:41:59,263 --> 00:42:02,659
Scroll the focused tab into view and make scroll

692
00:42:02,659 --> 00:42:05,678
controls named native buttons if they are needed.

693
00:42:05,678 --> 00:42:09,829
The extra controls should not cause the arrow handler to treat

694
00:42:09,829 --> 00:42:13,603
them as tabs or hide selected tabs from assistive technology.

695
00:42:13,603 --> 00:42:16,622
Test touch, keyboard, narrow layouts, and right-to-left direction.

696
00:42:16,622 --> 00:42:20,774
A visual overflow solution should preserve the widget's semantic interaction model.

697
00:42:22,149 --> 00:42:24,382
A11Y-003 · Follow-up 3

698
00:42:25,507 --> 00:42:29,350
Would you build this on the CDK's FocusKeyManager?

699
00:42:29,350 --> 00:42:34,154
What would it give you and what would it cost?

700
00:42:39,222 --> 00:42:44,715
FocusKeyManager can manage active items, wrapping, orientation, disabled skipping, and typeahead depending on configuration.

701
00:42:44,715 --> 00:42:47,069
It can reduce bespoke traversal code.

702
00:42:47,069 --> 00:42:50,208
You still own tab semantics, selected state, panels,

703
00:42:50,208 --> 00:42:52,954
identifiers, rendering, and automatic versus manual activation.

704
00:42:52,954 --> 00:42:56,486
It also introduces an adapter contract and a CDK

705
00:42:56,486 --> 00:42:59,624
dependency that must fit the supported framework range.

706
00:42:59,624 --> 00:43:03,156
Use it when the shared behavior outweighs that cost,

707
00:43:03,156 --> 00:43:07,472
and test the complete component rather than assuming the manager supplies

708
00:43:07,472 --> 00:43:08,257
accessibility automatically.

