00:48:59,685 --> 00:49:01,593
A11Y-004 · Fixed version

814
00:49:02,718 --> 00:49:06,440
The error paragraph is always rendered (empty when there is no

815
00:49:06,440 --> 00:49:09,825
error), so the live region exists before its text changes.

816
00:49:09,825 --> 00:49:13,210
It is only referenced from aria-describedby while it has content.

817
00:49:14,585 --> 00:49:17,972
A11Y-004 · What a strong candidate also mentions

818
00:49:19,097 --> 00:49:24,121
When to show errors is a product decision the library must support, not make.

819
00:49:24,121 --> 00:49:28,069
Showing an error on the first keystroke is hostile; the usual

820
00:49:28,069 --> 00:49:32,017
pattern is after the field is left (touched) or after submit.

821
00:49:32,017 --> 00:49:34,529
The component receives error as an input,

822
00:49:34,529 --> 00:49:37,042
which keeps that decision with the consumer,

823
00:49:37,042 --> 00:49:39,554
and the documentation should recommend a default.

824
00:49:39,554 --> 00:49:43,861
On submit, the form, not the field, should move focus to the

825
00:49:43,861 --> 00:49:47,809
first invalid field or to an error summary at the top.

826
00:49:47,809 --> 00:49:50,680
The library can provide a helper for this.

827
00:49:50,680 --> 00:49:54,269
Announcing every keystroke's validation through the live region is noisy.

828
00:49:54,269 --> 00:49:58,935
Debounce the error or only set it on blur. - autocomplete must be

829
00:49:58,935 --> 00:50:03,242
passable to the inner input (autocomplete="email"), for WCAG 1.3.5 (Identify Input Purpose).

830
00:50:03,242 --> 00:50:07,190
That is a reason to consider the attribute-selector design in API-002.

831
00:50:08,565 --> 00:50:10,627
A11Y-004 · Follow-up 1

832
00:50:11,752 --> 00:50:15,321
Why do many screen readers ignore a live region that

833
00:50:15,321 --> 00:50:18,534
is inserted at the same time as its text?

834
00:50:23,803 --> 00:50:27,681
Assistive technology often observes changes to an already registered live region.

835
00:50:27,681 --> 00:50:31,559
If the region and its first message appear in one insertion,

836
00:50:31,559 --> 00:50:35,790
some combinations treat it as initial content rather than an update to

837
00:50:35,790 --> 00:50:36,142
announce.

838
00:50:36,142 --> 00:50:40,726
Keep a persistent empty region, then change its text after the relevant interaction.

839
00:50:40,726 --> 00:50:45,309
Timing varies across platforms, so a delayed write is not a universal guarantee.

840
00:50:45,309 --> 00:50:48,130
Verify the DOM sequence automatically and test announcements

841
00:50:48,130 --> 00:50:50,950
with the supported browser and screen reader combinations.

842
00:50:52,326 --> 00:50:54,465
A11Y-004 · Follow-up 2

843
00:50:55,590 --> 00:50:58,511
Should the error be announced politely or assertively?

844
00:50:58,511 --> 00:51:01,067
What changes if you get it wrong?

845
00:51:06,459 --> 00:51:11,094
Polite is usually appropriate for field validation while the user is entering data.

846
00:51:11,094 --> 00:51:16,086
Assertive can interrupt the current speech and should be reserved for genuinely urgent information.

847
00:51:16,086 --> 00:51:20,722
Repeated assertive errors on every keystroke can make a form difficult to use.

848
00:51:20,722 --> 00:51:23,931
Decide when errors become visible, connect the error as

849
00:51:23,931 --> 00:51:26,783
a description, and avoid announcing unchanged messages repeatedly.

850
00:51:26,783 --> 00:51:29,636
Submission may need an error summary and deliberate

851
00:51:29,636 --> 00:51:32,489
focus management instead of several competing live announcements.

852
00:51:33,864 --> 00:51:36,118
A11Y-004 · Follow-up 3

853
00:51:37,243 --> 00:51:40,248
How would this component expose the inner input

854
00:51:40,248 --> 00:51:43,254
to consumers who need autocomplete, inputmode or maxlength?

855
00:51:48,667 --> 00:51:52,928
Prefer a form-field that wraps a projected native input enhanced by

856
00:51:52,928 --> 00:51:56,801
a directive, so native attributes stay on the real control.

857
00:51:56,801 --> 00:52:00,675
The field and directive can share a control interface through

858
00:52:00,675 --> 00:52:04,161
dependency injection and register label, helper, and error identifiers.

859
00:52:04,161 --> 00:52:09,584
If an internal input is necessary, document explicit attribute forwarding and a focus API.

860
00:52:09,584 --> 00:52:14,233
Do not assume arbitrary attributes on the wrapper automatically reach the descendant.

861
00:52:14,233 --> 00:52:17,332
Include autocomplete and forms integration in consumer examples.

