1023
01:01:59,179 --> 01:02:02,477
How would you test that a toast is announced?

1024
01:02:07,889 --> 01:02:11,164
Automate the structural contract: a persistent connected live region,

1025
01:02:11,164 --> 01:02:15,167
the intended politeness, and the new message reaching it after the

1026
01:02:15,167 --> 01:02:15,530
event.

1027
01:02:15,530 --> 01:02:19,170
Spy on a live announcer at a unit boundary only

1028
01:02:19,170 --> 01:02:22,809
when testing the call contract; also exercise the browser integration.

1029
01:02:22,809 --> 01:02:26,084
A DOM test cannot prove the exact spoken output,

1030
01:02:26,084 --> 01:02:29,723
so include manual screen reader checks for repeated messages, interruption,

1031
01:02:29,723 --> 01:02:30,451
and timing.

1032
01:02:30,451 --> 01:02:34,453
Document the tested combinations rather than declaring announcement behavior universally certified.

