01:16:11,997 --> 01:16:16,331
What breaks, and how would virtual scrolling interact with aria-activedescendant?

1262
01:16:21,742 --> 01:16:25,285
Rendering ten thousand options can cost layout and memory,

1263
01:16:25,285 --> 01:16:28,828
but virtualization can remove the element referenced by aria-activedescendant.

1264
01:16:28,828 --> 01:16:33,159
Keep the active option rendered or provide a compatible identity strategy,

1265
01:16:33,159 --> 01:16:37,884
and expose position and set-size information where the virtualized pattern requires it.

1266
01:16:37,884 --> 01:16:41,034
Coordinate scrolling and rendering before assigning the reference.

1267
01:16:41,034 --> 01:16:46,152
Test navigation across window boundaries, typeahead to offscreen items, and screen reader behavior.

1268
01:16:46,152 --> 01:16:49,302
Consider filtering or a native control before adding

1269
01:16:49,302 --> 01:16:52,058
complexity that the task does not need.

